# The scout moves twice, one step at a time, because territory 1 does not touch territory 3.
#
# **A second test, added by adding a file.** Nothing in `tests/` or `src/` names it.
#
# **The refresh between them is not decoration.** A scout has one move, so crossing two borders in
# one go is exactly what the allowance forbids - and this test would have been the first casualty
# of that rule. It now says what crossing twice costs.

{test name:the-scout-crosses-two-borders}

{given}
{territory id:1 name:territory-1}
{territory id:2 name:territory-2}
{territory id:3 name:territory-3}
{adjacency id:1 from:territory-1 to:territory-2}
{adjacency id:2 from:territory-2 to:territory-3}
{scout where:territory-1 moving:1} -> 1

{when}
{move what:scout from:territory-1 to:territory-2}
{refresh where:territory-2 what:scout trait:moving}
{move what:scout from:territory-2 to:territory-3}

{then}
{territory id:1 name:territory-1}
{territory id:2 name:territory-2}
{territory id:3 name:territory-3}
{adjacency id:1 from:territory-1 to:territory-2}
{adjacency id:2 from:territory-2 to:territory-3}
{scout where:territory-3 moving:0} -> 1
